	The nethack sources come configured with the system wizard
(presumably the person who maintains the sources) as "izchak".  Thus,
unless the WIZARD define is changed to a new name, a person gets into
DEBUG mode by the command:

nethack -uizchak -D		(in that order)

	However, for those people compiling with the KR1ED option (for
some early K&R compilers) this define defaults to "johhny".  So if you
want to get into DEBUG mode, you must type:

nethack -ujohnny -D

	I was unable to get into DEBUG mode on my Manx compiled
Nethack until Ken Lorber imformed me of this "feature".  Thanks to the
responsiveness and intelligence of the development team, the default
WIZARD will always be "izchak" in patchlevel 8.  Thanks Ken!
